    "body": "Note that what Firefox implemented is specifically that form submissions under a load event handler running do a replace load.  Doing things like `click()` on `<a>` elements does not, I'm pretty sure, because the relevant part of the code runs async in that case, so no longer under the load event (unlike form submission, which runs that code sync).\r\n\r\nI don't know that we've tested what Edge and Chrome do with `click()` here.",
